    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Missed Call → Instant Text-Back\nWhen you can't pick up, the caller instantly gets a friendly text from your business number — so they message you instead of calling your competitor.\n\n### Setup\n1. Buy a phone number in Twilio (or port your existing one). Add a **Twilio** credential in n8n and select it on *Text the Caller Back*.\n2. Fill in **Config**: your mobile number (`forwardToPhone`), your Twilio number (`twilioFrom`), ring time and text message. Use `+countrycode` format.\n3. Add a **Telegram** credential and chat ID (see workflow 09) — or delete the Telegram node.\n4. **Activate** the workflow, open *Incoming Call (Twilio)* and copy its **Production URL**.\n5. In Twilio Console → Phone Numbers → your number → *Voice Configuration*: set **A call comes in** → *Webhook*, paste the URL, method **HTTP POST**. Save.\n6. That's it — the second webhook (*Call Ended*) is called by Twilio automatically (the TwiML uses a relative URL, so no extra setup).\n\nFull guide: README.md in this workflow's folder.",
        "height": 564,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "038b9718-fae4-5302-a9d7-07ceba5a8488",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        20
      ]
    }
